  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-47066" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Organization for Migration (IOM)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Border Personnel&#x2019;s Capacities to Respond to and Mitigate the Spread of COVID-19</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM has developed training curricula and aids to enhance member states officials&#x2019; capacities to continue to work and to adapt their operational practices to the context of COVID-19 response at points of entry (PoE). This training curriculum draws upon the latest IOM and WHO reference materials, including International Health Regulations (IHR) (2005) on PoE preparedness and response.  In order to increase capacities for Border Agency personnel to be able to manage the current pandemic, a migration training curriculum will be developed that will utilize materials for remote training, as in-person support is not possible. This will be done by creating virtual classroom environments or self-paced e-learning courses, available on an online platform. Promotional material will also be designed on the correct process for dealing with the current COVID-19 pandemic, the correct use of protective equipment and how to minimize risk.</narrative>
  </description>
